cpcbuild patch for Caprice32 (ColinPitrat/caprice32 6c12c4c, GPLv2 like Caprice32).

Bug: Caprice32 keeps the Plus ASIC's DMA registers (&6C00-&6C0B address and
prescaler, &6C0F DCSR) in the ASIC register page buffer, but several places
write them through membank_write[], i.e. into whatever is mapped at
&4000-&7FFF. With the ASIC page out that is program RAM: every raster
interrupt ORs &80 into RAM at &6C0F, and every DMA cycle rewrites &6C00-&6C0B
and &6C0F. This corrupted Starfall Plus's code at one memory layout.

Fix: read and write those registers in pbRegisterPage (the register page
buffer) instead. Behaviour with the page in is unchanged.

Apply from the Caprice32 root: git apply tools/caprice32/caprice32-asic-regs.patch

diff --git a/src/crtc.cpp b/src/crtc.cpp
--- a/src/crtc.cpp
+++ b/src/crtc.cpp
@@ -678,8 +678,9 @@
          z80.int_pending = 1;
          asic.raster_int_pending = true;
          // Set the bit for the raster interrupt in DCSR.
-         word dcsr_addr = 0x6C0F;
-         *(membank_write[dcsr_addr >> 14] + (dcsr_addr & 0x3fff)) |= 0x80;
+         // (in the ASIC register page, not in whatever is mapped at &4000:
+         // with the page out that is RAM, which must not change)
+         pbRegisterPage[0x6C0F & 0x3fff] |= 0x80;
       }
       if (GateArray.hs_count) { // delaying on VSYNC?
          GateArray.hs_count--;
